welcome to the Slow Mo
Guys video all about,

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:18.140
how a pinball machine works.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.660
Firstly, I wanna say thanks
to Jersey Jack Pinball,

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.680
for providing the machine for this video.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:24.850
It's a Willy Wonka machine,

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:25.683
it's very nice,

00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:26.516
very colorful.

00:00:26.516 --> 00:00:28.280
I've been fascinated by pinball,

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.280
for quite a long time.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.520
I was introduced to a real pinball machine

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.000
by a Canadian man named Ed,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:34.900
before that,

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.630
my entire experience with pinball

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.770
was the significant
percentage of my childhood

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:41.941
taken up by this.

00:00:46.861 --> 00:00:48.070
And even though we live in the future now

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:51.200
well beyond the days of
electromechanical scoring,

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.390
the actual play field itself,

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:55.720
uses components unchanged for decades

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.310
it's still very mechanical

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:58.210
and not only that,

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.700
very fast moving,

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.600
so why don't we whip out the phantom

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.110
and play a little game of pinball.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:04.750
Since I got this machine,

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.280
I've played a lot of Wonka Pinball,

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.060
and I've determined some
areas of the play field

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.020
that I wanna feature,

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.460
but it's gonna be an extremely fiddly job

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.650
so I've got the Flex4K
with the pro blends on

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:17.610
and I'm gonna use that with
this extremely bright light,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.020
to really get in there.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.100
Okay, the glass is off

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.180
I think we should start with me

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.640
just playing a cheeky game of pinball

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:24.880
just you can see everything that moves

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.950
and then we'll get in there
for the slow-mo replays.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.790
The game is fully
functional without the glass

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:30.930
and now there's no glare for filming.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:31.950
However,

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.830
I'm slightly worried about
taking a pinball to the chin,

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.990
because they do go flying,

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.470
in multiball especially

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:39.720
and also without the glass,

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.300
something that I wasn't expecting

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.510
this machine is now,

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.230
incredibly loud.

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:45.063
There is a,

00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:47.480
I guess a huge sound dampening
effect with the glass cover

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.823
so, get ready for some clangs and clunks.

00:01:51.782 --> 00:01:52.710
I'm not sure if you knew this about me

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:55.390
but I'm actually phenomenal at pinball

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:57.390
I'm really good at,

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.930
from this flipper hitting it

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:01.810
so that it bounces off this target here,

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:05.140
and drains about 165 miles an hour

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.580
that's probably my specialty

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:07.413
all right,

00:02:07.413 --> 00:02:08.246
high score coming up.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:11.793
In all seriousness

00:02:11.793 --> 00:02:13.580
I'm a total pinball novice,

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:14.710
so apologies in advance

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.510
for my sorry display of skills

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.840
and potential incorrect terminology.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.673
Starting with a gobstopper

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:23.050
if you hit it once it will
spin around revealing a hole

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.910
and then you can hit a ball
in locking it for multiball,

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:26.820
it's actually a virtual lock

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.310
it's not keeping the balls physically

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.320
it pops them back out
into the shoot again,

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.153
just there,

00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:33.830
but one other ways to build multiballs,

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:35.870
is to activate various locks,

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:37.050
now we're in the pot bumpers,

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.420
at the top I'm sure you've seen these,

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.177
on a pinball machine
extremely fast moving,

00:02:40.177 --> 00:02:41.750
extremely loud,

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.720
down here if the pink light is lit

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.330
the kickback will prevent the ball

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.360
from draining on the outer lane there,

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:48.200
when it's not lit

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.160
you lose the ball.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.080
Locked another ball for multiball
there in the gobstopper.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.670
When the yellow light in
the center middle is lit

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:58.340
the ball will be diverted
from the gobstopper ramp

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.610
down onto magnet

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.040
to be hit through the spinner

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.700
and when the super lock light is lit

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.290
that will lock a ball for
the Wonka Vater multiball

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:06.470
which as this machine

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:08.580
is the standard version is a virtual lock

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.800
on the limited edition,
collector's edition

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:11.980
this is a physical lock

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:13.320
that sits at the back there

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.300
and it will physically store your balls

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.630
before dumping them
back onto the playfield.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.370
As you can see now I'm in,

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.420
what I like to call slingshot hell,

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.700
where my ball is just
bouncing back and forth

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.860
between the slingshots,

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.850
finally gain control,

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.130
started gobstopper multiball,

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:29.030
locked three balls

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:32.750
and all three are now auto
plunged back onto the playfield.

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.050
Multiball still freaks me out

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.100
even if I know what I'm
supposed to be aiming at,

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:36.933
just the fact that

00:03:36.933 --> 00:03:38.090
there's so many balls in the playfield

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.630
and you still have to keep your eye on

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.370
when a ball is about to
hit the upper flippers

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:43.300
and the lower flippers,

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.330
it's a lot to look at,

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.163
and it didn't help here

00:03:45.163 --> 00:03:47.420
that I actually started a second multiball

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.290
a kid multiball within
the gobstopper multiball,

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:51.730
which crossed all six balls

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.860
to be on the playfield at the same time,

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.070
there's a lot going on.

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.090
This is actually a,

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.950
a montage of several different
moments from the same,

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.103
play session,

00:04:01.103 --> 00:04:02.941
but there are bits cut just to,

00:04:02.941 --> 00:04:05.580
show different stuff
happening a lot quicker.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.083
So we can get to the slow motion.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.670
If you get the high score,

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:25.530
when you submit your name

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:26.480
it'll take a picture of your face

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.430
and you'll hear a little
funk inside the machine

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:29.368
which we'll get to later.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:31.820
Grand champion.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:32.653
To fully show

00:04:32.653 --> 00:04:33.920
how this machine works,

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:34.870
we're gonna to need to film

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:35.880
underneath the play field

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.570
and thankfully you can
just pull it out like this

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:40.230
and everything is still fully functional

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:41.750
I can activate pretty much everything,

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.530
you're also able to push it up fully,

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.690
the most common way for something

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.200
to move on the pinball machine

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.527
is through switches and solenoids,

00:04:48.527 --> 00:04:50.240
and you can see a few of them here.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.610
This empty gap in the bottom left

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:54.010
that's where the Wonka
Vater ball lock would be,

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:55.510
if I had that version of the game.

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:57.381
A solenoid is basically
very tightly coiled wire

00:04:57.381 --> 00:04:58.214
which when a current passes
through create a magnetic field,

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.560
pulling the metal rod through the center,

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:03.530
this one is the flipper

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.073
and this one is the vertical up kick

00:05:05.073 --> 00:05:06.150
when the ball trough,

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.910
responsible for deploying balls,

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.260
and they work very quickly.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.420
So why don't we get straight into slow-mo,

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.770
starting with the vertical up kicker,

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:14.770
of the ball trough.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:15.710
Pressing the start button,

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.520
hits the switch which activates

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:18.917
the vertical kick trough,

00:05:18.917 --> 00:05:23.706
firing the ball straight
up into the shooter

00:05:23.706 --> 00:05:24.730
while roll down,

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:27.050
and it's ready to be plunged,

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:27.913
by the plunger.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:34.640
On a full plunge,

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.780
the ball will go right round the top,

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.780
straight into the pot bumpers

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:39.890
this was the part of the machine

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:41.000
I was most excited to see

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:44.490
just because the ball so
quickly bounces back and forth

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.680
between these multiple times per second,

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:47.680
you can see the way it works

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.081
is when the ball rolls
over the white plastic

00:05:50.081 --> 00:05:52.650
the rod connected to the metal ring above

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:55.370
is pulled down by solenoid inside

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.710
so when it rolls over the white plastic,

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.030
this leaf switch completes the circuit,

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.733
activating solenoid

00:06:01.733 --> 00:06:02.800
that pulls this rod down

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.460
and that is connected to the ring above

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:06.680
on the top of the play field

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.240
and the way the ring is angled

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.860
'causes the ball to be ejected out

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:13.190
from any angle that it
approaches the pot bumper

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.200
you can see it now,

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.200
activating switch,

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.180
rod pulls down,

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.760
ball fires back out.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:20.370
It bounces seriously fast,

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:23.000
I counted here that the
ball went back and forth

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.860
eight times in less than half a second,

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.410
absolutely insane.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:29.580
Now heading down to the flippers,

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.530
classic area of a pinball machine

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.430
as you can see

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:33.700
press the button,

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:34.780
flipper moves,

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:35.830
hits the ball away

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.970
it's a very strong mechanism

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:41.750
and there are actually two
circuits regarding the flipper,

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.210
it's a solenoid once again,

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.980
actuating in this arm,

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:46.950
there's a circuit for the initial,

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:48.490
high power burst of current

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.760
which is needed to move it

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.850
and then a separate lower power circuit

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:53.530
to hold the flipper in place

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.640
if you wanna hold it up,

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.440
just so you're not running high current

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:57.540
through it constantly.

00:06:59.881 --> 00:07:02.845
The spring will return it
to its resting position,

00:07:02.845 --> 00:07:05.360
when you physically press
the flipper a button,

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.890
a little piece of plastic
is pushing against,

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:10.430
metal leaf switches inside,

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:11.930
when one piece of metal
knocks into another

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:12.970
it completes the connection.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:13.803
You may be wondering

00:07:13.803 --> 00:07:14.950
why is there three?

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:17.150
You can actually press just the first one

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.334
that activates the lower flipper,

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.110
when the first piece pushes

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:23.300
the second piece of metal
into the third piece,

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.680
the entire circuit is complete

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:25.770
and the upper flipper

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:26.920
goes as well.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.550
Usually both flippers go at the same time

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.870
'cause you're really smashing these things

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:31.040
this is the slingshot

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.560
slightly above the lower flippers.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.718
You'll notice two leaf
switches either side,

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.220
of this kicker also powered
by a solenoid inside

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.860
when the ball approaches from
either side of that thing

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:41.850
it will complete the circuit

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.690
causing the ball to be kicked out,

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.659
often straight into the other one

00:07:45.659 --> 00:07:46.920
which causes a nice,

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.180
back and forth between them.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.350
This is the gobstopper hole,

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:50.270
when a ball goes in

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:51.720
as I mentioned before the ball is locked

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.230
but it's actually just returned to you

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:55.460
through this plastic channel underneath

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:58.980
and then using another vertical up kicker,

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:01.090
is shot straight back up

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:04.110
and that is the ball that
you continue playing with.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.400
Comes out just slightly
higher up the shooter lane,

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:08.530
then where the ball starts originally.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:09.710
When multiball starts the game,

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.630
will just launch balls
onto the play field for you

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:12.508
using the auto plunger.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.240
This piece of metal is shaped to come out

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:16.960
either side of the normal plunger,

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:18.620
whacking the ball at full speed,

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:19.893
back up the shoot again.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.720
When you hit the ball
up the gobstopper ramp,

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:48.510
the ball can either
continue straight through,

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:50.760
depending on where you are in the game

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:53.400
or if the yellow light
is lit on the left there,

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:56.550
once the ball is detected
using the optical sensors,

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:59.770
this divert a piece of metal
will come down from the top,

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:01.670
slowing the ball down enough

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:03.620
for it to just drop through

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:04.500
this hole in the side.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.670
If the ball is traveling full speed

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.190
it never falls down there.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:08.620
The ball then fall down,

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:09.740
onto a magnet,

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:12.540
where it's ready to be hit
by the upper left flipper,

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:13.710
into the spinner,

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:15.580
for usually some mad points.

00:09:18.099 --> 00:09:20.240
'Cause every full rotation,

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:23.050
it activates this leaf switch

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:23.980
on the right here,

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:24.813
so you can see

00:09:24.813 --> 00:09:25.730
if you hit it through there

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:27.360
and it spins 40 times

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:29.420
this switch repressed 40 times

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.390
which could mean 41 Cuba's

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:33.090
if you've got super spinner activated,

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.480
now we're into some multiball,

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:35.930
I'm honestly so surprised

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.160
at how often the ball

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:38.220
just leaps into the air

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.433
sometimes it will hit the glass

00:09:39.433 --> 00:09:40.410
when you're playing.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.600
Up here in the center is the captive ball

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.890
which operates exactly
like a Newton's cradle

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:48.020
you have to hit the ball
hard enough for it to send

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.050
the fireball into the target.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.177
Basically just to target
you have to hit pretty hard.

00:09:52.177 --> 00:09:55.430
Now one of these balls is
gonna drain out of the,

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:56.860
left outer lane,

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.770
which is the one that has the kickback

00:09:58.770 --> 00:09:59.850
which when lit,

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:03.020
if the ball rolls over
this metal roll over switch

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:06.370
is automatically bashed straight back out

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.810
and your ball is saved.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:09.297
I spent a lot of time
filming this machine,

00:10:09.297 --> 00:10:11.359
one of the most fascinating
parts of it to me,

00:10:11.359 --> 00:10:14.270
was something I noticed when
I was filming the flippers,

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:17.310
the ball is rarely hit just once,

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:21.610
the first impact almost stops
the flipper and the ball,

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:23.130
and then as it catches up

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:25.420
it then does a secondary push

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:27.030
or secondary hit to the ball,

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:27.890
and not only that,

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:31.090
without a ball the flippers
decelerate so fast,

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:34.330
that it ripples the rubber
away from the plastic,

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:36.670
this all occurs in around 0.1 of a second

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:39.500
so incredibly difficult
to see with the naked eye.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.040
First, I thought something was wrong,

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.380
until I noticed this behavior
on every single flipper

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:44.550
even the upper one here,

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:47.540
such force the rubber
completely comes away,

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.500
in my quest to become better at pinball,

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.560
I was learning about a
move called a live catch

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:52.393
where you sort of

00:10:52.393 --> 00:10:54.480
meet the ball right as
it lands in the flipper

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:56.940
and they sort of both cancel
out each other's momentum.

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:57.773
It's I guess,

00:10:57.773 --> 00:10:59.870
like the closest to a real
life frame perfect trick

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:01.010
that there is in pinball.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:01.843
So I was thinking

00:11:01.843 --> 00:11:03.040
maybe the rubber whipping away

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.510
from the plastic on the flipper

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:07.800
actually extends the possible
window of a live catch

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:10.240
because it's literally
extending the flipper itself

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:12.080
and cushioning all around the ball,

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:13.850
it's actually not a good
example of a live catch

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:16.160
'cause the ball still just
rolled off the flipper

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.170
usually it's meant to just,

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.360
stop dead on the flipper

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.470
and then you haven't caught.

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.260
Now let's move on to the tilt bob,

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:23.690
it sits inside this machine on the left

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:25.440
as you can see it's swinging,

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:27.610
loosely and it's got a ring surrounding it

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:28.720
so you can see here when I,

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:29.580
nudge the machine

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.560
give a little tilt to
try and save the ball,

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.120
it gave me a warning

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:35.460
'cause it detected that the
tilt bob had hit the ring,

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:36.690
and it is a big part of the game,

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:38.710
sort of smack the machine around

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:40.410
but if the bob hits the ring three times,

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:41.370
you get a tilt,

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:42.320
you lose your current ball

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:43.905
and lose your bonus.

00:11:43.905 --> 00:11:44.738
Finally,

00:11:44.738 --> 00:11:45.571
we have the knocker,

00:11:45.571 --> 00:11:46.910
it sits in the back box

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:48.150
so I've got to take this part off

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:49.190
and it's the thing you hear

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:50.460
when you get high score,

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:52.000
or if you roll over the special,

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:55.010
and it's just a solenoid
with a plastic tip rod

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:56.783
that thumps a piece of metal.

00:11:58.213 --> 00:11:59.046
Incredibly simple.

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:01.090
Well there we have it

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:03.070
I honestly found that so interesting,

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:05.110
just shoving the camera
in different spots,

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:06.870
and learning how each piece worked,

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.760
just from the footage alone,

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:09.710
found it fascinating,

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:10.830
I really enjoyed that one,

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:11.940
hopefully you enjoyed it too

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.330
even if you're not into pinball

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:15.220
maybe you found it interesting anyway,

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:17.900
big fat thanks to Jersey Jack pinball,

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:20.100
for supplying this wonderful machine

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:21.830
and honestly supplying me with a new hobby

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:25.200
I've been in here almost
every day for the last month,

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.510
just trying to get into Wonka's office

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:27.343
haven't done it yet

00:12:27.343 --> 00:12:28.320
it's actually,

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:30.780
it's an easy game to sort of get going on

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:32.610
but it's a lot deeper than you think

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.330
there's actually a tonne to do

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.730
and I'm really just
scraping the surface on it.

